# sgo.build — DIFF-RETAINS-REPRO. Does `Diff.diff` retain the trees it walks?
# The wata-mac idle leak bisected to the diff call: with it skipped the live
# heap is flat, with it running — nothing encoded, nothing handed to the
# backend — every frame's view tree stays reachable. This module is the
# standalone arbiter: wataui's differ, a loop, and a heap probe, with NO app
# around it. If a bare loop leaks here, the retaining edge is below
# wataui/diff.scala and the finding goes upstream to sgola.
mode app
emitname diff-spike
binname diff-spike
gomod diffspike
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/memprobe ../go-pkgs/memprobe
